# cmd's prompt on the bottom row, a full-screen program starts, the window
# grows (a maximize), the program redraws and exits. Measured
# (vim-maximize-powershell, altscreen-maximize-powershell): ConPTY's main
# buffer keeps its rows where they were and adds blank rows below, so the
# shell's next absolute write goes to the old prompt row.
size 80 20
pty conpty
seq L 1 40
send \r\nsync>
send \e[?1049h\e[H\e[2JFULL SCREEN
resize 80 29
send \e[H\e[2JFULL SCREEN
send \e[?1049l
expect xfail F015 (PKG-14): the grid growth pulls scrollback into the active area
|L23
|L24
|L25
|L26
|L27
|L28
|L29
|L30
|L31
|L32
|L33
|L34
|L35
|L36
|L37
|L38
|L39
|L40
|
|sync>
end
cursor 5 19 xfail F015 (PKG-14): the grid growth pulls scrollback into the active area
send \e[20;6Hecho synced
expect xfail F015 (PKG-14): the grid growth pulls scrollback into the active area
|L23
|L24
|L25
|L26
|L27
|L28
|L29
|L30
|L31
|L32
|L33
|L34
|L35
|L36
|L37
|L38
|L39
|L40
|
|sync>echo synced
end
